cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ExtProbe"
type: software
abstract: >-
  ExtProbe is an open-source dynamic-analysis tool for Chrome Manifest V3
  extensions. It runs an extension in an instrumented, containerized Chrome
  and records what the extension actually does at runtime (network requests,
  DOM changes, opened tabs and API use), attributing each event to the
  extension component that caused it. It produces an explainable report and a
  risk score to help analysts review extensions before installation. An
  optional probe mode (--probe) opens the extension's own pages and safely
  exercises their controls to elicit behavior gated behind user actions.
